    "part-s": "STM32N657Z0H3Q",
    "description-s": "STM32N657Z0H3Q is a high-performance microcontroller based on the Arm 32-bit Cortex-M55 core with TrustZone, running up to 800 MHz (overdrive), 1280 DMIPS, with 32-Kbyte ICACHE/DCACHE, MVE and Helium technology, and an FPU. It integrates the ST Neural-ART Accelerator (neural processing unit) running up to 1 GHz at 600 Gops for deep-neural network inference, a Neo-Chrom 2.5D GPU, hardware JPEG codec with MJPEG, an H264 video encoder, an ISP (image signal processor) with parallel/2-lane CSI-2 camera interfaces, and an LCD-TFT controller. Memory includes 4.2-Mbyte contiguous SRAM, 128-Kbyte TCM RAM with ECC plus 64-Kbyte instruction TCM RAM with ECC, 8-Kbyte backup SRAM (VBAT), and a flexible external memory controller (FMC) supporting SRAM/PSRAM/SDRAM/NOR/NAND plus two XSPI ports up to 200 MHz. Security features include Arm TrustZone, SESIP Level 3/PSA certification, secure boot, HUK secure storage, two AES coprocessors, PKA, HASH, and a true RNG. Communication peripherals include 2x USB 2.0 HS OTG (one with USB Type-C Power Delivery), 10/100/1000 Ethernet with TSN, 4x I2C Fm+ + 2x I3C, 6x SPI, 2x SAI, 5x USART/5x UART + 1x LPUART, 2x SDMMC, and 3x FDCAN. It offers up to 165 GPIOs, two 12-bit ADCs up to 5 Msps, a temperature sensor, and operates over an industrial temperature range of -40 to 125 degC. This variant is offered in the VFBGA142 (8x8 mm, 0.5 mm pitch) package with the internal SMPS step-down converter dedicated pinout option.",
